body:
Looks good to me.

- C# code needs few changes to use new API names:
```diff
diff --git a/modules/mono/editor/GodotTools/GodotTools/Export/ExportPlugin.cs b/modules/mono/editor/GodotTools/GodotTools/Export/ExportPlugin.cs
index cb20290792..ae5a142182 100644
--- a/modules/mono/editor/GodotTools/GodotTools/Export/ExportPlugin.cs
+++ b/modules/mono/editor/GodotTools/GodotTools/Export/ExportPlugin.cs
@@ -406,7 +406,7 @@ namespace GodotTools.Export
                                 {
                                     if (platform == OS.Platforms.iOS && path.EndsWith(".dat", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
                                     {
-                                        AddIosBundleFile(path);
+                                        AddAppleEmbeddedPlatformBundleFile(path);
                                     }
                                     else
                                     {
@@ -453,7 +453,7 @@ namespace GodotTools.Export
                     throw new InvalidOperationException("Failed to generate xcframework.");
                 }
 
-                AddIosEmbeddedFramework(xcFrameworkPath);
+                AddAppleEmbeddedPlatformEmbeddedFramework(xcFrameworkPath);
             }
         }
 
```
- And there's a small issue with `generate_bundle`.

_Release management note (This is not something that should be addressed in the PR): Official build scripts should be updated to match env variable/command line argument name changes. I have not tested building with `osxcross` container, but changes in the iOS build should not affect it in any significant way. Not sure if it can build for visionOS at all, so it likely will need some reorganization if we want to ship official export templates._
